ary we found stand  firmly uh with our nato allies and our  support of nato and the the wider  defense agenda you know it is unwavering  as the labour party  yeah i'm not asking you to make any  decisions obviously that's not for you  but would you support do you think we're  entering a dangerous period in  you know western russian relations where  we should all be thinking about  increasing defense spending now well  absolutely i mean this is one of the  most  i think terrifying eras uh of of my  lifetime you know i never  we didn't ever think did we as a  generation that we would see such a  blatant um breach of of those  international norms that we've we've  been living with for decades now with a  an illegal invasion on a european uh  country on our doorstep by russia and  that requires  that is going to require a radical  rethink in in terms of our  public policy our foreign policy our  defense policy and so on and you know i  think  uk  nato the west we are  really waking up to to that that new  threat and um you know we have  a united  agenda here now i think we have seen  tough action but it could be tougher  still and and we want we want the uk  government we want other governments to  go further when it comes to those  economic sanctions tackling the  oligarchs that take safe haven in our  country and when it comes to things like  sporting and cultural  sanctions and also  increasing that that military aid  directly into ukraine so that the  ukrainian people can defend  a themselves word on sport i mean sport  does appear as if it's  um stepping up to the plate on this what  more would you want um sporting bodies  and cultural organizations to do  well we are seeing some moves in the  right direction with uefa  and to some degree with with fifa  football and others but i think we need  to send a clear and categoric message  that russia from now on will be fully  excluded uh fully uh boycotted from all  international sporting and cultural  events so things like the upcoming world  cup uh it shouldn't be a case that  russia can still take part be it with  without  displaying its country's name they  should be excluded from that event  without delay uh we've got the the  women's euro finals taking place here in  the uk in the summer the same two world  chess championships  they're still hosting international  volleyball and swimming competitions  later this year i think we now need to  see a full and clear categoric signal  so that putin who takes these occasions  very seriously when he's hosting or when  he's participating uh in these events he  needs to feel the full force of that  where it hurts and it will send a strong  signal to the russian people as well  that they need to stand up to to putin  because they'll no longer be able to  take pride in in their country taking  part in such events  okay lucy powell thanks very much
 

